\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 I guess one last fun thing we could do is, would you like to propose (actually one-shot generate) a working CLI solution / script that spawns and generates a git repo per day of livestreaming to serve as backbone for daily piece accumulation and hash/diff/change management, something that perhaps even plays nice with OBS, but not necessarily? (In any case though, provide a place to generate a proper identifier plus hashtree for a given day's livestream metadata overlay as well as place to dump the machine readable event logs etc?) Assume I am a computer scientist (with general amnesia), I favor rust for PROD apps, python for complex app prototyping, bash otherwise for scripting, and the idea is to push repos to github in tandem with large file pushing / streaming to youtube/huggingface/substack.\
\
This we could think of as a fun Astra capabilities test with minimal input context / poorly specified build intention.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
